    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22338" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλῠκ-άζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sweeten</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν κατάποσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epict.
					<u>Gnom.</u>
					22
				</span></i>
			; <i>affect with a sensation of sweetness</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς ὑγιαίνοντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>P.</u>
					1.211
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>receive a taste of sweetness</i>, Hierocl.<i><span class="en">
				p.29A.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>P.</u>
				1.20
			</span></i>; but, <i>taste sweet,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gp.
				2.39.4
			</span></i>, and so intr. in 
				Act.
			 of wine, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				1.26c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλι γλυκάζον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Ez.</u>
					3.3
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				4.3.26
			</span></i>.</div>
